\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Calibrated panoramic depth for the Rainier capture, near field bright. Two properties discussed above are visible directly. The near-field meadow is resolved in detail, while everything from the mid-ground treeline outward collapses into a narrow band of values: the raw prediction has saturated, and the far-range compression maps that whole range onto the approach to $D_{\max }$. The sky is masked out rather than assigned a depth.}}{10}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rainier-depth}{{3}{10}{Calibrated panoramic depth for the Rainier capture, near field bright. Two properties discussed above are visible directly. The near-field meadow is resolved in detail, while everything from the mid-ground treeline outward collapses into a narrow band of values: the raw prediction has saturated, and the far-range compression maps that whole range onto the approach to $D_{\max }$. The sky is masked out rather than assigned a depth}{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{fig:rainier-depth@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][10][]10}{}{}{}}
